bbcode_enabled = true
bbcode_text = "[b]Privacy Notice[/b]
Caesar is a modular, open-source management software for Minecraft servers, licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3). As such, it is provided without any warranty – use it at your own risk.

[b]Data Usage[/b]
Upon first start, Caesar will send a single HTTP request to [color=blue][u]https://ipinfo.io[/u][color=white] to determine your approximate location (based on IP address). This data is used only locally to enhance your user experience by displaying:

• Current weather
• Local time
• Time zone

on the [b]Dashboard.[/b]
[b]No data is stored or transmitted[/b] beyond this inital request. Your location is [b]never[/b] sent to our servers, nor is it used for analytics or shared with third parties.

This feature can be disabled at any time in the settings under [code]Dashboard → Local Enhancements[/code].

[b]Legal Note[/b]
Caesar is released under the GPL v3 license, meaning:

• You are free to use, modify, and distribute it.
• The software comes as-is, without any warranty, expressed or implied.
• The developers of Caesar cannot be held liable for any damage, data loss, or other issues resulting from its use.


We believe in openness, transparency, and user control. You can always inspect the full source code at [color=blue]https://github.com/JWeinelt/Caesar[color=white]."
text = "Privacy Notice
Caesar is a modular, open-source management software for Minecraft servers, licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3). As such, it is provided without any warranty – use it at your own risk.

Data Usage
Upon first start, Caesar will send a single HTTP request to https://ipinfo.io to determine your approximate location (based on IP address). This data is used only locally to enhance your user experience by displaying:

• Current weather
• Local time
• Time zone

on the Dashboard.
No data is stored or transmitted beyond this inital request. Your location is never sent to our servers, nor is it used for analytics or shared with third parties.

This feature can be disabled at any time in the settings under Dashboard → Local Enhancements.

Legal Note
Caesar is released under the GPL v3 license, meaning:

• You are free to use, modify, and distribute it.
• The software comes as-is, without any warranty, expressed or implied.
• The developers of Caesar cannot be held liable for any damage, data loss, or other issues resulting from its use.


We believe in openness, transparency, and user control. You can always inspect the full source code at https://github.com/JWeinelt/Caesar."

